sentences.t:
miseris heu praescia longe
horrescunt corda agricolis, dabit ille ruinas
arboribus stragemque satis, ruet omnia late;

sentences.l:
for the wretched, alas, foreknowing far off,
shudder the hearts of the farmers; it will bring downfall
to the trees and havoc to the crops, it will overthrow all things far and wide;

sentences.t:
Ferit ense gravem Thymbraeus Osirim,
Archetium Mnestheus, Epulonem obtruncat Achates
Ufentemque Gyas;

sentences.l:
Thymbraeus with his sword strikes heavy Osiris,
Mnestheus Archetius, Achates cuts down Epulo,
and Gyas Ufens;

sentences.t:
Occidis, Argivae quem non potuere phalanges
sternere nec Priami regnorum eversor Achilles;
hic tibi mortis erant metae:

sentences.l:
You fall, whom the Argive could not phalanxes
lay low, nor of Priam's kingdom the overthrower, Achilles;
here for you of death were the turning-posts:
